KG42.register("rules-5f50a657a7739d745981c708",{"id":"10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R007","paper":"10-hierarchical_coordination","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R007","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local energy product","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The local energy product is the energy purchased from or sold to other prosumers in the local market, distinguished from energy exchanged with the grid. Scope: First-stage local P2P energy market; each prosumer, time slot and scenario.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function product.local_energy under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["product.local_energy"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"First-stage local P2P energy market; each prosumer, time slot and scenario.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g02-e05"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R007-x1","symbol":"P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega}","meaning":"Energy quantities of bidding for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega, i.e. the local energy purchased from other prosumers in the first-stage P2P market; the local-purchase component of the prosumer's total purchased energy.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy quantity (kWh) for each prosumer j, time slot t and scenario \\omega; the source declares it a first-stage variable of the prosumer decision problem. No explicit numeric bound on this specific symbol is stated in the supplied evidence.","unit":"kWh","indices":["j","t","\\omega"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-en3","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g01-e08"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R007-x2","symbol":"P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega}","meaning":"Energy quantities of offering for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega, i.e. the local energy sold to other prosumers in the first-stage P2P market; the local-sale component of the prosumer's total sold energy.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy quantity (kWh) for each prosumer j, time slot t and scenario \\omega; the source declares it a first-stage variable of the prosumer decision problem. No explicit numeric bound on this specific symbol is stated in the supplied evidence.","unit":"kWh","indices":["j","t","\\omega"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-en3","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g01-e08"]}],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local energy product is the energy purchased from or sold to other prosumers in the local market, distinguished from energy exchanged with the grid. Scope: First-stage local P2P energy market; each prosumer, time slot and scenario.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g02-e05"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The local energy product is the local component of the prosumer's total traded energy: total purchased energy equals the energy purchased from other prosumers in the local market plus the energy purchased from the grid, and total sold energy equals the energy sold to other prosumers plus the energy sold to the grid (Eqs. (4)-(5)). Scope: each prosumer j, time slot t and scenario \\omega.","expression":"P^{-}_{jt\\omega} = P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} + P^{g,-}_{jt\\omega}, \\forall j, \\forall t, \\forall \\omega; P^{+}_{jt\\omega} = P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} + P^{g,+}_{jt\\omega}, \\forall j, \\forall t, \\forall \\omega","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R007-x1","v141-c-R007-x2"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g01-en3"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e03","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3","section":"2. Proposed local energy market model","anchor_text":"flexibility is defined as an electricity commodity which is provided by ty flexible power system pla","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"restatement"},"source_text":"According to our proposed LEM structure, in the first stage, prosumers are able to trade with each other in a P2P energy market, where the LMO is in charge of coordinating P2P tradings among them. In the second stage, the LMO in cooperation with the DSO dispatches the flexibility provided by prosumers considering distribution network constraints."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers","anchor_text":"energy exchanged with the grid as seen in Eqs. (4) and (5): 𝑃−𝑗𝑡𝜔= 𝑃𝑙𝑚,−𝑗𝑡𝜔 + 𝑃𝑔,−𝑗𝑡𝜔, ∀𝑗, ∀𝑡, ∀𝜔 (4","equation_id":"(4)-(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Thus, the total purchased/sold energy of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega can be defined which is splitted to the local energy traded with other prosumers and the energy exchanged with the grid as seen in Eqs. (4) and (5): P^{-}_{jt\\omega} = P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} + P^{g,-}_{jt\\omega}, \\forall j, \\forall t, \\forall \\omega   (4)   P^{+}_{jt\\omega} = P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} + P^{g,+}_{jt\\omega}, \\forall j, \\forall t, \\forall \\omega   (5)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e08","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":"4","section":"2.1.1. Bidding strategy for prosumers","anchor_text":"work for energy and flexibility trading in the LEM. LEM which are obtained based on prediction by pr","equation_id":"(4),(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"P^{-}_{jt\\omega} = P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} + P^{g,-}_{jt\\omega}, \\forall j, \\forall t, \\forall \\omega \\qquad (4)\nP^{+}_{jt\\omega} = P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} + P^{g,+}_{jt\\omega}, \\forall j, \\forall t, \\forall \\omega \\qquad (5)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-en3","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p02-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":2,"printed_page":"2","section":"Nomenclature","anchor_text":"𝑡 g g 𝜆−𝑡 ToU buying price from the grid at time slot 𝑡 𝐿𝑗 Maximum energy consumption for pro- sumer","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Parameters in the first stage: \\beta_{jt} Portion of interruptible loads for prosumer j at time slot t which is between 0 and 1; \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} Predicted energy trading price in the LEM for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; \\lambda^{+}_{t} ToU selling price to the grid at time slot t; \\lambda^{-}_{t} ToU buying price from the grid at time slot t; \\bar{L}_{j} Maximum energy consumption for prosumer j; \\bar{P}_{j} Maximum energy generation (PV capacity) for prosumer j; \\rho_{\\omega} Probability of scenario \\omega; L_{jt\\omega} Energy consumption for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P_{jt\\omega} Energy generation for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega. Variables in the first stage: \\lambda^{p2p}_{jit} The price of P2P energy trading between prosumers j and i at time slot t; \\lambda^{b}_{jtm} Bidding price of prosumer j in block m and time t; \\lambda^{o}_{jtm} Offering price of prosumer j in block m and time t; O_{jt} Offer vector for prosumer j at time t; B_{jt} Bid vector for prosumer j at time t; B_{jtm} Bidding quantity of prosumer j in block m and time t; O_{jtm} Offering quantity of prosumer j in block m and time t; EC^{p}_{j} Expected cost for prosumer j; EP^{p}_{j} Expected profit for prosumer j; Lf,i_{jt\\omega} The amount of interruptible load for prosumer j at time t and scenario \\omega; Lf,s_{jt\\omega} The amount of shiftable load for prosumer j at time t and scenario \\omega; OF^{p}_{j} Objective function for prosumer j; P^{p2p,+,bl}_{jitm} The quantity of offering for P2P trading among prosumers j and i at time slot t and block m; P^{p2p,+}_{jit} Energy that prosumer j sells to prosumer i at time slot t; P^{p2p,-,bl}_{jitm} The quantity of bidding for P2P trading among prosumers j and i at time slot t and block m; P^{p2p,-}_{jit} Energy that prosumer j buys from prosumer i at time slot t; P^{+}_{jt\\omega} Total energy sold of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{-}_{jt\\omega} Total energy purchased of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{g,+}_{jt\\omega} Energy sold to the grid at ToU price by prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{g,-}_{jt\\omega} Energy purchased from the grid at ToU price to prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} Energy quantities of offering for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} Energy quantities of bidding for prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega; u_{jit} A binary variable representing P2P trading status between prosumers j and i at time slot t; v_{jt\\omega} A binary variable for expressing status of buying/selling in the LEM of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":"This rule defines a traded-energy product and the supplied source evidence introduces no fixed numeric constants or parameters specific to it. The symbols j, t and \\omega appearing in the rule scope are indices/sets (prosumers, time slots, scenarios), not parameters, so theta is empty. The predicted LEM price and ToU prices appear in Eqs. (2)-(3), which belong to the prosumer bidding objective rather than to this product definition, so they are not declared here."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M04-coordination","v141-a-M04-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","quote":"the total purchased/sold energy of prosumer j at time slot t and scenario \\omega can be defined which is splitted to the local energy traded with other prosumers and the energy exchanged with the grid"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e03","quote":"According to our proposed LEM structure, in the first stage, prosumers are able to trade with each other in a P2P energy market"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"aaf88337b9484ce4791004b4a2ffcdddac9c9482a791d493b51dcbaeca046feb","applicability":"formalized","reason":"This rule governs the local energy product and source evidence supplies an actual defining expression. v141-b-g02-e05 and v141-b-g01-e08 transcribe Eqs. (4)-(5), which define the energy traded with other prosumers (P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega}, P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega}) as the local component of the prosumer's total purchased/sold energy, and v141-b-g01-en3 declares these as first-stage variables indexed by prosumer, time slot and scenario. These support a formal mathematical definition (new constraint v141-c-R007-C002). The existing C.1 constraint C001 is retained unchanged as the procedural market-meaning statement. Evidence remains UNREVIEWED under the experiment's source-review policy (no B audit, no scientific acceptance).","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-x1","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} is the local purchased-energy quantity that instantiates product.local_energy, i.e. the 'energy purchased from other prosumers' named by this rule's market meaning. Same mechanism v141-a-M01; supported by v141-b-g01-en3 (nomenclature) and v141-b-g02-e05 / v141-b-g01-e08 (Eqs. (4)-(5)). The frozen graph supplies no edges for this rule, so no edge binding is possible."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-x2","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} is the local sold-energy quantity that instantiates product.local_energy, i.e. the 'energy sold to other prosumers' named by this rule's market meaning. Same mechanism v141-a-M01; supported by v141-b-g01-en3 (nomenclature) and v141-b-g02-e05 / v141-b-g01-e08 (Eqs. (4)-(5)). No edges exist in this rule's frozen graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The decomposition Eqs. (4)-(5) formalizes product.local_energy as the local (prosumer-to-prosumer) component of the prosumer's total traded energy, distinguished from grid energy. It is bound to the only node of this rule; E = [] so no edge binding is available."}],"revision_requests":["Source decomposition Eqs. (4)-(5) (v141-b-g02-e05, v141-b-g01-e08) also reference the total purchased/sold quantities P^{-}_{jt\\omega}, P^{+}_{jt\\omega} and the grid-traded quantities P^{g,-}_{jt\\omega}, P^{g,+}_{jt\\omega}. These are not nodes, variables or parameters of the frozen rule v141-c-R007 (V = [product.local_energy], E = [], x = [], theta = []). If the local energy product must be defined strictly relative to these companion quantities, C.1 should confirm whether additional nodes/edges (or a link to the bidding rules v141-c-R001/v141-c-R002) are required; the definition is transcribed here using only the local-product symbols as this rule's declared variables.","The frozen graph for v141-c-R007 contains no edges (E = []) and no declared x/theta. No source relation connecting product.local_energy to another approved node was supplied, so no edge-level formalization was performed; if such a source relation exists, C.1 re-extraction is required.","The symbols P^{lm,-}_{jt\\omega} and P^{lm,+}_{jt\\omega} are also used by the prosumer bidding rules (v141-c-R001 bidding.demand, v141-c-R002 bidding.supply) within the same mechanism v141-a-M01. They are declared here only under this rule's explicit source scope (each prosumer, time slot and scenario); any cross-rule reuse must rely on that explicit scope and not on cross-round inference, since the graph does not represent whether these quantities are shared or distinct across rules.","Under the experiment's source-review policy, evidence v141-b-g01-e03, v141-b-g02-e05, v141-b-g01-e08 and v141-b-g01-en3 remain UNREVIEWED (native source_status unverified, no B transcription audit and no independent scientific acceptance). This C.2 formalization is therefore provisional, and its exact expression, symbol domains and unit assignment (kWh) should be re-checked once B source verification is available."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
